## Task 9B3 authoritative panel artifact codec

Commit `3d2b4bab0635627ffd0ef75b9aced38ca1413bf8` (`fix(pit-v5): authenticate legacy
panel artifacts`) fixes the incompatible panel serialization boundary. The dedicated repository
loader authenticates the contained raw file and its reference digest, rejects duplicate keys and
inexact nested schemas, reconstructs `EvaluationPanelSpec`, and requires an exact round trip through
the same newline-bearing serializer that defines `EvaluationPanelSpec.sha256`. It additionally
requires `panel.sha256 == reference.sha256`; panel identity and the generic V5 codec are unchanged.
`LocalSandboxMountFactoryV5.panel_for` now selects this dedicated loader.

The same correction covers CLI readiness graph traversal. Only the exact panel-plan reference in
a strictly decoded authenticated `CampaignManifestV5`, followed by the episode panel references in
its strictly decoded `CampaignPanelPlanV5`, selects panel authentication. Episode dates, lineages,
purpose, and digest must match. Every ordinary graph edge retains generic V5 authentication, even
when it aliases an already verified panel. Completion records include the traversal role while the
returned authenticated graph remains deduplicated. Filenames and caller-selected artifact types
cannot opt an ordinary edge into the legacy codec.

The focused verification commands and results were:

- `python -B -m py_compile core/pit_optimizer_v5/artifacts.py core/pit_optimizer_v5/production_sandbox.py` — passed.
- `python -m ruff check core/pit_optimizer_v5/artifacts.py core/pit_optimizer_v5/production_sandbox.py` — `All checks passed!`.
- `python -m ruff format --check core/pit_optimizer_v5/artifacts.py` — `1 file already formatted`.
- The broader format check identified existing formatting drift in `production_sandbox.py`; a
  separate `git show HEAD:core/pit_optimizer_v5/production_sandbox.py` piped through Ruff's stdin
  format check also returned 1 before this commit. Its unrelated formatting and dirty hunks were
  preserved. Only `artifacts.py` was formatted.
- `git diff --check -- core/pit_optimizer_v5/artifacts.py core/pit_optimizer_v5/production_sandbox.py`
  and `git diff --cached --check` — passed (the former emitted the existing Windows LF-to-CRLF advisory).
- `python -B -c "p=r'.artifacts/task9b3_panel_codec_smoke.py'; exec(compile(open(p, encoding='utf-8').read(), p, 'exec'), {'__file__': p})"`
  passed before and after the commit hooks with these exact results:
  `PIT_V5_PANEL_CODEC_OK valid=quick,discovery factory=integrated digest_rejections=2 noncanonical_rejections=8 malformed_rejections=16 episode_binding_rejections=8 generic_codec=unchanged`
  and
  `PIT_V5_PANEL_GRAPH_OK valid_nodes=16 panel_nodes=6 invalid_graphs_rejected=11 ordinary_codec=strict panel_route=authenticated_manifest_plan_edges`.
- The 11 rejected graphs cover newline-free, noncanonical, malformed, and digest-mismatched panels;
