## Task 9B3 production factory and fresh-process bootstrap

Commit `f995525ad507fa3a5c10c313ac24d44d120e345c` (`feat(pit-v5): bootstrap
production runtime`) removes the process-local production-factory registry and constructs the
closed concrete V5 graph directly from an authenticated adapter-config artifact. Run and resume
now bind the exact local artifact repository, provider ledger/audit/gateway, one-shot role runner,
Git materializer, sandbox mount factory, container executor, panel/probe evaluator, candidate-base
operations, request/novelty/record/archive factories, monotonic clock, cancellation, and composite
owned cleanup. Composition rechecks the complete concrete alias and identity graph before entering
the accepted runtime. OpenRouter retries and schema-repair calls remain zero, and the fixed
`OPENROUTER_API_KEY` environment handle is resolved only at the actual one-shot invocation.

The sandbox mount factory no longer reads PIT bundle bytes during construction. It binds the
authenticated logical data authorities and pinned data-root identity at construction, then checks
the exact two-file layout, bounded hashes, and issued file identities while the data directory and
files are held for an actual panel transaction. Semantic probes continue to receive no PIT-data
mount or handle. Verify and summarize reconstruct only the smallest read-only authorities needed
to authenticate the event/payload chain, candidate-execution index, role ledger/accounting,
checkpoint/experiment set, archive projection, and cleanup records.

