## Task 9B3 retirement-index recovery fix round 2

Commit `5a56874cc762831ab6997f4d550fa12f5c43d3cc` (`fix(pit-v5): recover orphan
workspace retirement indexes`) addresses the remaining P1 against base
`b378ca5700cc484953da7a482724b833aa2c9441`. Operational cleanup recovery now has a
separate `recover_lease_history` path serialized by the exact workspace transition. It first
authenticates the immutable reservation, creation/readiness records, exact owner/root/token/lease
bindings, and workspace absence. Only the exact missing retirement-index reference derived from
that independent authority can enter recovery. The repository recovery primitive authenticates
the already-existing retirement bytes against that expected value and publishes only their missing
create-only index; it never creates or replaces value bytes or repairs an unrelated index.

The existing read-only `authenticate_lease_history` route and all verification state reads retain
`repair=False`. Indexed-but-missing values, noncanonical/tampered/foreign orphan values, conflicting
authority, missing prerequisite indexes, and reappearing workspaces cannot trigger index repair.
The earlier removed-before-retirement window still returns `removed` without manufacturing a
retirement value. Composite cleanup rejects a foreign round before entering operational recovery.

The temporary deterministic fake ran as
`python -B .artifacts/task9b3_retirement_index_smoke.py` and reported exactly:

```text
