PIT_V5_RETIREMENT_INDEX_RACE_OK conflicting_publication=rejected overwrite=0
```

It exercised the real repository typed decoding, canonical byte/digest authentication, index
loading, and recovery logic against an in-memory byte store. It reproduced value publication
without index publication, proved read-only verification fails without writing, observed one exact
index creation during composite recovery, and repeated recovery/verification three times without
another write. Negative cases also covered a conflicting index appearing at create-only
publication. The fake rejected all generic `repair=True` reads and any value or unrelated index
write. It was removed before staging; `Test-Path` returned `False`.

